1. git init  -> making the curent directory as the working directory
2. git add . -> adding all the files in the staging area,
4. git commit -m "message"-> commts done
5, git status -> any files are in workng dir, staging area.
6. when we modify the code, it again goes to untracked area.
7. git restore --staged names.txt -> moves the file to normal area.
8. git log -> list all the commits.
9. git stash pop -> come out.
10. git stash clear -> to clear the chqanges in the stash area.
11. git remote add 	origin <link-of-your-git repository>.git
12. git remote -v ==> this lists all the origins attached to your working directory.
13. git push origin master => code is pushed to the master branch.
14. git branch branch_name
15. git checkout branch_name --> switched to the branch_name.
16. git fetch --all prune -> fetches all the brances along with deleted comits
